      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a start, but it feels a bit too academic. I'm looking for the \"killing blow\" arguments. For example, isn't it true that their entire economic model fundamentally ignores human nature—specifically the fact that people won't work hard if the state just takes everything? If I'm trying to frame this as an inherently failed or even dangerous ideology to the average voter, what are the most mathematically or logically undeniable ways their platform falls apart?",
