      "content": "The argument that strong state intervention fundamentally misjudges human self-interest is a powerful one to leverage. You can argue that in a system where the state heavily dictates outcomes, the powerful \"moral hazard\" is that the strong right to support, regardless of contribution, undermines the strong will to produce in the first place. This can be framed as a guaranteed \"unintended consequence\" where high support leads to systemic dependency and a decline in the overall work ethic necessary for a strong, free economy.",
